00:21:04.370 --> 00:21:05.210
Justin Florentine: Okay.

179
00:21:05.330 --> 00:21:11.210
Justin Florentine: What do you see being different from a, you know, managing roles and permissions perspective?

180
00:21:12.840 --> 00:21:14.740
Ry Jones (The Linux Foundation): It makes it much easier.

181
00:21:15.590 --> 00:21:24.250
Ry Jones (The Linux Foundation): Mostly because the, the last radius of any changes is limited to one project.

182
00:21:25.880 --> 00:21:26.600
Ry Jones (The Linux Foundation): Yes.

183
00:21:27.380 --> 00:21:37.500
Ry Jones (The Linux Foundation): you have a… if someone is able to compromise or do something to the configuration of the Hyperledger org, it doesn't affect

184
00:21:37.770 --> 00:21:41.249
Ry Jones (The Linux Foundation): other orgs. It doesn't affect other projects, as of, for instance.

185
00:21:42.190 --> 00:21:50.839
Ry Jones (The Linux Foundation): It also, really helps in terms of, Cost and, spend allocation.

186
00:21:51.830 --> 00:21:54.789
Ry Jones (The Linux Foundation): So, if you are using large runners.

187
00:21:55.160 --> 00:21:59.679
Ry Jones (The Linux Foundation): We can put a specific org on a specific budget, so that

188
00:21:59.950 --> 00:22:07.570
Ry Jones (The Linux Foundation): when they run out, they run out. They don't run the whole org out. Right now, that's,

189
00:22:07.990 --> 00:22:10.379
Ry Jones (The Linux Foundation): Partially the case, but not completely the case.

190
00:22:11.030 --> 00:22:11.900
Ry Jones (The Linux Foundation): So…

191
00:22:14.770 --> 00:22:15.600
Justin Florentine: Okay.

192
00:22:16.030 --> 00:22:21.579
Justin Florentine: I'll go ask around our team members, see if anybody else has any questions on the matter.

193
00:22:21.690 --> 00:22:26.219
Justin Florentine: I personally am more comfortable with it.

194
00:22:26.710 --> 00:22:32.430
Justin Florentine: So, I wouldn't… I wouldn't mind maybe kicking off the new year with this migration.

195
00:22:33.770 --> 00:22:35.150
Ry Jones (The Linux Foundation): That would be awesome.

196
00:22:38.390 --> 00:22:41.030
