201
00:23:05.580 --> 00:23:10.409
Matthew Whitehead (Kaleido): So, no, no big concerns from us. I know…

202
00:23:10.410 --> 00:23:32.849
Matthew Whitehead (Kaleido): I know Paladin, for example, pulls in stuff from BESU, not… not from the Besu fork, from the open source repo. We'll spot that if there are issues. I think it's just Maven coordinates we pull in, so if redirects work, then that's great. If we need to change something in Paladin, that's not a big deal. It's only for our… well, no, that's not true. It's not only for our test infrastructure. But, yeah.

203
00:23:34.730 --> 00:23:45.609
Matthew Whitehead (Kaleido): it will be useful for us to keep abreast of when that shift happens, but we will, we'll spot any issues where redirects aren't working, or where we need to make a small PR to pick up a different Maven

204
00:23:46.100 --> 00:23:51.400
Matthew Whitehead (Kaleido): you know, I don't know if we'll need to pick up a different Maven, coordinate or anything.

205
00:23:51.740 --> 00:24:00.440
Justin Florentine: I don't think so, I think those are just things that we manage with our own package management system, and it's a different notion of an organization, so…

206
00:24:00.850 --> 00:24:01.860
Justin Florentine: Yep.

207
00:24:02.050 --> 00:24:06.989
Justin Florentine: There may be some changes in the future, but they would be detached from this initiative.

208
00:24:07.380 --> 00:24:07.890
Matthew Whitehead (Kaleido): Yeah.

209
00:24:10.250 --> 00:24:11.010
Justin Florentine: Cool.

